<h3 class='sec-banner' style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;padding-bottom:4px;page-break-after:avoid;'>Section A: Multiple Choice Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;margin-bottom:8px;page-break-after:avoid;'>Note: Choose the correct option for each of the following questions.</p><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q1.</strong> Which Java package automatically imports the standard library classes like Integer, Character, and Double? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) java.util</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) java.io</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) java.lang</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) java.awt</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q2.</strong> What is the process of automatic conversion of a primitive data type into its corresponding wrapper object called? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Explicit Casting</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Autoboxing</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Unboxing</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Parsing</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q3.</strong> Which of the following methods converts a numeric String "250" into a primitive int? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Integer.valueOf("250")</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Integer.parseInt("250")</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Integer.toString("250")</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) String.valueOf(250)</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q4.</strong> What will be the return type of `Character.isDigit(char ch)`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) char</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) int</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) String</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) boolean</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q5.</strong> Which wrapper class corresponds to the primitive data type `char`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Char</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) String</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Character</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Text</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q6.</strong> What will be the output of `Character.toUpperCase('b')`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) 'B'</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) true</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) 'b'</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) 66</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q7.</strong> What is the output of `Character.isWhitespace(' ')`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) false</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) true</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) 32</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) null</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q8.</strong> Which of the following is NOT a wrapper class in Java? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Byte</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Short</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Float</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) double</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q9.</strong> What will happen if you execute `Integer.parseInt("12A")`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Returns 12</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Returns 0</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Throws NumberFormatException</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Throws NullPointerException</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q10.</strong> The conversion of an object of a wrapper class back to its corresponding primitive value is known as: </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Autoboxing</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Unboxing</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Typecasting</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Widening</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q11.</strong> What is the return type of `Double.parseDouble(String s)`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Double</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) double</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) float</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) String</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q12.</strong> Which method of `Character` class checks if a character is either a letter or a digit? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Character.isLetterOrDigit(char ch)</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Character.isAlphaNumeric(char ch)</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Character.isLetterAndDigit(char ch)</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Character.checkLetterDigit(char ch)</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q13.</strong> What is the result of `Character.isLowerCase('7')`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) true</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) false</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) 7</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Compilation Error</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q14.</strong> Which of the following statements correctly demonstrates explicit unboxing? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) `Integer obj = 10;`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) `int x = obj.intValue();`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) `String s = Integer.toString(10);`</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) `Integer obj = Integer.valueOf(10);`</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q15.</strong> Which method is used to convert an integer primitive value into a String representation? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Integer.parseInt(int i)</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Integer.toString(int i)</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Integer.toInteger(int i)</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) String.toInt(int i)</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q16.</strong> All wrapper classes in Java are: </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Mutable</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Immutable</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Abstract classes only</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Interfaces</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q17.</strong> What will `System.out.println(Character.toLowerCase('A'));` print? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) A</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) a</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) true</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) 97</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q18.</strong> Where are wrapper class objects allocated in memory? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Stack Memory</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Heap Memory</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Class Register</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Read-Only Memory</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q19.</strong> What is the return type of `Integer.valueOf("100")`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) int</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Integer</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) String</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) float</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q20.</strong> What is the output of `System.out.println(Character.isLetter(''));`? </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) true</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) false</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Exception</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) </li></ul><h3 class='sec-banner' style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;padding-bottom:4px;page-break-after:avoid;'>Section B: Fill in the Blanks</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;margin-bottom:8px;page-break-after:avoid;'>Note: Fill in the blanks with appropriate terms or Java expressions.</p><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q1.</strong> The process of automatically wrapping a primitive type into a wrapper object is called _______. </div><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q2.</strong> The static method used to parse a String into a primitive float value is _______. </div><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q3.</strong> All library wrapper classes are available in the default package named _______. </div><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q4.</strong> The method `Character.isLetterOrDigit('7')` returns the boolean value _______. </div><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q5.</strong> Automatic conversion of a wrapper object back into its corresponding primitive type is called _______. </div><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q6.</strong> To convert a lowercase character variable `ch` to uppercase, we use the statement `ch = _______(ch);`. </div><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q7.</strong> Wrapper class objects are stored in _______ memory area in Java. </div><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q8.</strong> The return type of `Character.isLetter(char ch)` is _______. </div><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q9.</strong> Executing `Integer.parseInt("12.34")` throws a _______ exception. </div><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q10.</strong> Wrapper objects in Java are _______, meaning their contents cannot be altered after creation. </div><h3 class='sec-banner' style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;padding-bottom:4px;page-break-after:avoid;'>Section C: True / False</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;margin-bottom:8px;page-break-after:avoid;'>Note: State whether the following statements are True or False.</p><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q1.</strong> Wrapper classes are imported explicitly from `java.util` package. </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q2.</strong> Autoboxing is performed automatically by the Java compiler without needing explicit casting. </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q3.</strong> `Character.isDigit('A')` returns true. </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q4.</strong> Primitive data types do not possess built-in utility methods, whereas Wrapper classes do. </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q5.</strong> All wrapper objects in Java are immutable. </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q6.</strong> `Integer.parseInt("100")` returns an object of `Integer` class. </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q7.</strong> `Character.toLowerCase('9')` returns '9'. </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q8.</strong> Primitive type `double` has wrapper class `Double`. </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q9.</strong> `Character.isWhitespace('\t')` evaluates to false. </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul><div class='q-item' style='margin-bottom:10px;page-break-inside:avoid;'><strong>Q10.</strong> `Character.isLetter('_')` returns true because underscore is treated as an alphabetic symbol. </div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>True</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>False</li></ul>
